abstract: This dataset contains salmon stomach content data collected by the CCGS
  Sir John Franklin in the Eastern Gulf of Alaska in March 2022. These data were collected
  as part of the International Year of the Salmon (IYS) Winter Pan-Pacific High Seas
  Expeditions, to further improve the understanding of factors impacting salmon early
  marine winter survival. Salmon were caught with a midwater trawl and clustered in
  10cm size classes. Stomach content identified to the lowest taxonomic rank possible
  or practical. The dataset contains occurrence data of prey found in the stomachs
  of salmonids, as well as information on prey proportions, digestion levels (by prey)
  and the index of stomach fullness for the salmon.
